{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":91,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T02:41:27.068494728Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c70c494a-dd9f-48b2-ba5f-1384575eb5b4","comment_uuid":"26bd2b4f-907b-466e-9cac-f673f63d991d","author":"y4rr","content":"Plan: match PyTorch backward root semantics. Validate explicit external gradient shape/device first, then reject roots that neither require grad nor have a grad_fn; for implicit backward reject non-grad roots before scalar-ness. If the root is a requires_grad leaf, run the same grad-hook/post-accumulate path as normal leaf inputs and accumulate the seed directly instead of dropping it from the temporary grad map. Add scalar, [1]-shape, vector external-gradient, error-precedence, hook, repeated-accumulation, and CUDA-residency tests.","created_at":"2026-06-16T02:41:27.065944112Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAiM7bHVdnm6O0J+FWFtsMLYUpzsZTwzHpmTtNVsOKotdn4nHXWzGe72WDdnAg2FUDuDMSC65rRTk/u2A3jZ8YDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPvrkwFEeLx/mwpAqI+Mms2tA6IYZx3BWHe+l1BsagjrODp39W1yyiRKbxJGgxXO0PweerI5raHbwLbOgFEm3w8="}
{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":92,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T02:49:02.212284462Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f782351c-bf81-4132-b84a-7508adc788a7","title":"Backward skips register_hook on non-leaf root tensors","description":"While fixing CORE-037 leaf-root backward, code inspection against PyTorch showed the root seed path also skips Tensor::register_hook for non-leaf roots. PyTorch applies a hook registered on y to the initial seed before y.grad_fn runs; e.g. y=(x*x), y.register_hook(lambda g: g*5), y.backward() makes x.grad=20 when x=2. Ferrotorch only ran hooks when a tensor appeared as an input to another grad_fn, so hooks on the root output were ignored.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"c70c494a-dd9f-48b2-ba5f-1384575eb5b4","created_by":"y4rr"},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOVCeYWJW7AtZlidJgeYUZCexfgULW/NYxyS8xNmkjXQz5rk3slb0qfDc3G4VI5eaggQnnISfo7GjvueTyBPowQ="}
