{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":116,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T03:23:10.948775507Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ee1fffea-500f-46c0-b03f-24db6c9af84d","comment_uuid":"90ecde6c-7d4d-44df-a4fc-0856c7d8c2f0","author":"y4rr","content":"Plan after code inspection + live PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130 probe: PyTorch rejects every value/index selecting dim reduction when shape[dim] == 0, even if another non-reduced zero would make the output empty ([0,0,3] dim=1 errors). It accepts empty outputs only when the reduced dimension is nonzero and a non-reduced dimension is zero ([0,2,3] dim=1 -> [0,3], [0,2,0] dim=1 -> [0,0]). Existing ferrotorch guards incorrectly key some ops on outer*inner != 0, and the f32 CUDA amin/amax wrapper uses inner.max(1), which corrupts valid empty-output decomposition. I will make reduced-dim zero an unconditional InvalidArgument for argmax/argmin, max/min(dim), median/nanmedian, preserve valid empty outputs, and add CPU/CUDA regression probes.","created_at":"2026-06-16T03:23:10.946380931Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAilM41TKkxMsyCt1qTnjxB5LcMVomkYcdG45CR52zbld7ZtArjkCYMwgt6f1IQOOuv0labgx1ImBpfSYEOPWnCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDOKftk+1YJztElgO/nB2K3wg6tgAdagpvru2QB9Wun/ppeUSJwfZo3gHv2RP0Bc/lh2i4angttZE8D+0jSsSw4="}
