{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":157,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T04:55:08.063644984Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7ed037cf-f0d2-4e0e-a258-75381373bd09","comment_uuid":"22fab7ff-13ec-4bdc-8f21-4bc0e992c940","author":"y4rr","content":"Current-state verification in session #198: inspected ferrotorch-core/src/sparse.rs and local PyTorch /home/doll/pytorch/torch/sparse/semi_structured.py. PyTorch to_sparse_semi_structured validates dimensional shape constraints and rejects [2,2] instead of grouping across rows; live probe on local torch: to_sparse_semi_structured(torch.ones((2,2), dtype=float16, device=cuda/cpu-selected)) raises RuntimeError 'shape torch.Size([2, 2]) is not supported'. Ferrotorch now rejects scalar inputs and any last dimension not divisible by 4 before reading data, so 2:4 groups cannot span rows/slices; sparse_matmul_24 independently enforces b.shape()[1] % 4 == 0. I also corrected a stale struct invariant doc that still described the old numel%4 contract. GREEN: cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --test audit_core075_24_innermost_dim_validation -- --nocapture => 4 passed; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --lib sparse -- --nocapture => 50 passed. Closing as implemented in current tree.","created_at":"2026-06-16T04:55:08.061261634Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAOlF7x7i3xnBpvXCGxYz7eKZ9hzVj44E6RYZUJLo2XSZRj5IhALrCJEPQQyhOz0ZgH25i1Ksa5IzaWD+mjGS1AA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK6KP/+9aLi4vp3wj+7OT9pLY9bSnCEudJOevSh6rUg7q2erUp2g7cfvEWhDS2zCYO2r26413YH1cGiRo6Hejg4="}
