{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":166,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T05:12:40.788346160Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad009906-8bcd-4dab-a08a-980bdcae2600","comment_uuid":"5d2260fd-9dac-43f8-bcdd-767d51e30a1a","author":"y4rr","content":"Discovered while fixing #1771. ferrotorch-core now validates sparse CUDA indices/dimensions before dispatch, but direct ferrotorch-gpu/src/sparse.rs callers still have a few allocation-before-dimension-check paths, e.g. gpu_coo_to_csr_indices returns vec![0; m + 1] for nnz==0 before i32::try_from(m), and CSR->CSC empty paths return vec![0; n + 1] before checking n. Harden wrappers to reject dimensions outside CUSPARSE_INDEX_32I/signed 32-bit range before any host/device allocation; add direct ferrotorch-gpu tests that do not allocate giant buffers.","created_at":"2026-06-16T05:12:40.785802175Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA61dM1NCaiqQ1/xqufk/JedKw2FffFmoCZXvY6p5dZSl2qXoZ2PMlwssj690Iy6Tor6GiYgkVQTIHrep16dJbCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHCw/QWCc3iQuDF/z0rfs9nfGned2mx/7t1MI2yLpPCxlfTn8wXLwC6Zfp6+SaNlFmsj1p/0a3hgyRF5+gq4XwU="}
{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":167,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T05:13:12.437994399Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"988da26f-2bc3-45c3-af24-e1207bcd3bda","comment_uuid":"888a372d-619e-4f4c-876a-434241596205","author":"y4rr","content":"CORE-077 tightened beyond the prior fix. Local PyTorch source checked: COO sparse indices are kLong in /home/doll/pytorch/aten/src/ATen/SparseTensorImpl.cpp, compressed sparse indices are Int or Long in /home/doll/pytorch/aten/src/ATen/native/sparse/SparseCsrTensor.cpp, and CUDA sparse paths use signed 32-bit casts for legacy cuSPARSE calls in SparseBlasImpl.cpp. ferrotorch's registered sparse GPU ABI stores u32 slices but passes them as CUSPARSE_INDEX_32I, so the safe bound is i32::MAX, not u32::MAX. Fix: to_u32_checked now rejects values above i32::MAX with structured InvalidArgument; all ferrotorch-core sparse CUDA entry points also validate row/column/inner dimensions before backend dispatch/allocation. Tests extended with i32::MAX+1 cases for COO column and row dimensions while preserving CPU acceptance of >u32 metadata. Evidence: cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --test audit_core077_sparse_u32_truncation -- --nocapture (1 passed); cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --features gpu --test audit_core077_sparse_u32_truncation -- --nocapture (7 passed); cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --features gpu --test conformance_nested_sparse -- --nocapture (37 passed); cargo fmt --check; cargo clippy -p ferrotorch-core --all-targets --features gpu -- -D warnings; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --lib (1733 passed). Commit: 1a8c85ce1. Adjacent direct ferrotorch-gpu wrapper hardening recorded as #1976.","created_at":"2026-06-16T05:13:12.435578084Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAVdI7IeSzQADBrrxHXt1fajMI7fYtvl5hv7cNh1cxabZ3A0I4