{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":205,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T06:33:51.398698727Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d5ead020-7d4a-4dfc-a7f5-ebc22863172c","comment_uuid":"f5eb71cc-3fe4-405e-920d-285fadee4e3e","author":"y4rr","content":"RESULT: fixed CORE-084 beyond the previous row-boundary patch. apply_2_4_mask now matches the public torch.ao.pruning.WeightNormSparsifier 2:4 shape contract: it accepts only non-empty 2-D weight tensors whose final dimension is divisible by 4, and returns structured InvalidArgument for rank-1, rank-3, empty dimensions, and bad row widths. CPU still builds row-local masks; CUDA now receives the same pre-kernel validation and has a regression for invalid CUDA shapes. The quantize_prune fixture generator no longer reshapes 1-D tensors into fake [1,n] oracle inputs; fixtures were regenerated from real PyTorch. Also opened related #1979 for the separate SemiStructuredSparseTensor/to_sparse_semi_structured shape-dtype conversion parity gap found during this sweep. Commit: 2981b6ba5 Enforce 2:4 pruning shape parity. Verification: python PyTorch probe for valid [2,4], invalid [4], [2,6], [0,4], [2,0], [2,2,4]; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --lib pruning -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --test conformance_quantize_prune -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --features gpu --test conformance_quantize_prune -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --lib semi24_compress_then_decompress_matches_apply_2_4_mask -- --nocapture; cargo fmt; cargo clippy -p ferrotorch-core --all-targets --features gpu -- -D warnings; git diff --check.","created_at":"2026-06-16T06:33:51.396341416Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA13Qr3KwejbrFm4L8b/bpLqoT22LiF5uqxchI8d4jkTrwKjANPffxTeaTT/4l1N2Xu40R4cAsx/hzNamGGCHLAg