{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":267,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T14:03:10.124241620Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"11f63203-b0be-4574-a3e8-245565381bfe","title":"CORE: Default RNG unit tests race under process-global RNG","description":"Full ferrotorch-core lib test runs can fail checkpoint RNG preservation tests even though the tests pass in isolation. After default CPU RNG moved to a PyTorch-style process-global generator, unit tests that assert exact manual_seed streams use crate::rng::default_rng_test_lock(), but unguarded unit tests that call creation::rand/randn can still consume the same global stream concurrently. Fix the unit-test-only RNG serialization so guarded exact-stream tests block all default RNG operations in the same test binary without changing production RNG semantics.","priority":"high","created_by":"y4rr"},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO5i2bzAWiJbi2FMzPEmbIGVbdugDuKD1/9iNIuMT6qClO6UUsncikQntFhrRPcKpEXW5iuMcRGvkIFg03UNHAw="}
