{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":283,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T16:36:00.007557892Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8333ffbe-a8a2-42bf-8003-5e8137bc2591","comment_uuid":"5bf134c7-53d4-4227-9293-a182d50bb517","author":"y4rr","content":"Plan: implement this as PyTorch runtime parity per backend. Local PyTorch 2.11 probe and source show CPU copy casts flow through c10::convert/static_cast, yielding target-width invalid sentinels and no range errors; CUDA uses device static_cast/PTX behavior, which intentionally differs for several invalid f32/f64 cases. Ferrotorch CPU currently does float -> i64 saturating Rust cast -> target try_from, which can yield zero or errors instead of the target-width PyTorch result. I will replace the CPU path with target-width conversion and pin all f32/f64/f16/bf16 to i32/i64 exceptional cases, while asserting CUDA outputs stay resident and match PyTorch CUDA.","created_at":"2026-06-16T16:36:00.004916016Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAWGdKCh4yUEtom0P3x1CEB4yZyhMYbr1yxNIHrkGtNyvOOnyRk+x7aL2PFyhVKYa2CFpLOlujknXpljiQzAupAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHmmQRj06bwpdYO8KYwngtMjUbxG9VPGz2Ewn85jBptbypInCo4addJHJnWdeWVrGVXuNLZ/AAF5UVmGXDs6XAc="}
