{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":293,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T17:54:41.438493940Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e1cc4479-ed5b-44eb-af20-85090ebc2e9a","comment_uuid":"7014176b-acb2-4a7e-9a2f-d1e8750fda06","author":"y4rr","content":"Result: resolved alongside CORE-116 after checking local PyTorch 2.11 behavior. PyTorch's CondAutogradOp/ScanAutogradOp still return requires_grad=True outputs when a tensor operand/input requires grad, even if the selected branch/step result is detached; backward writes explicit zero gradients to disconnected inputs. The fix therefore keeps higher-order output tracking but removes fake CPU rematerialization and adds zero-gradient edges for detached branch/step outputs. Verified with CPU detached-output probes and CUDA resident connected/detached/non-contiguous probes in audit_core116_117_higher_order_control_flow.","created_at":"2026-06-16T17:54:41.436103685Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAe3TMTZy9ClWpw5WuOWEitdX8gvcyCEf0K1xCc5kiZkgYPVjZ6uwoJm4P9dP98d9QpC6YZqj3iosjTK8m5JVyAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEeQbXvCcdWeJFb4pK3BR9CyjW6vZ12RZBrzCBYiosncbCzAVEAr0j7xHbipg0RwtH4t5F6lSGJCsbLkXO87Zw8="}
