{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":301,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T18:09:50.297499497Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9f7d1021-bbb3-4eb8-bc58-e5d37c671037","comment_uuid":"18b204fe-d5d6-41ac-942a-3e28559ddb7f","author":"y4rr","content":"Result: cond now evaluates scalar predicates through read_cond_predicate, which accepts 0-D or one-element tensors on CPU or CUDA. CUDA predicates use an explicit one-element data_vec synchronization instead of pred.data(), so callers no longer need to pre-copy selectors to CPU. The selector now matches local PyTorch 2.11 tensor truthiness: exact zero is false; nonzero values, including 0.25, 0.5, negative values, and NaN, are true. Verified with: python local PyTorch oracle probe; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --test audit_core119_cond_cuda_predicate -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --lib ops::higher_order -- --nocapture; CUDARC_CUDA_VERSION=13000 cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --features gpu --test audit_core119_cond_cuda_predicate -- --nocapture; CUDARC_CUDA_VERSION=13000 cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --features gpu --test audit_core116_117_higher_order_control_flow -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --lib; cargo fmt --all --check; git diff --check; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 cargo clippy -p ferrotorch-core --all-targets -- -D warnings; CUDARC_CUDA_VERSION=13000 CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 cargo clippy -p ferrotorch-core --all-targets --features gpu -- -D warnings.","created_at":"2026-06-16T18:09:50.295164665Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAe6ysSdlh26qAfeC5p0P+rS1OMihl3Umasi+IAnxH/6CJHmOKweoiMjtGSurr+c3XPsWls1RvyJ8hJ7TvYzcZDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AA