{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":318,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T19:47:19.179831777Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1cbe2a0-f4c4-4b35-b30b-2fbe693901bf","comment_uuid":"4a52b0c9-70c0-4710-84ed-925bdd263949","author":"y4rr","content":"Observation: live PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130 confirms matrix_rank is intentionally non-differentiable (int64 output, requires_grad=false), while ldl_factor preserves a grad edge on the factor output but raises 'derivative for aten::linalg_ldl_factor_ex is not implemented' on backward. I am treating those as the parity contract, not the original issue wording. Implemented build-outs so far: CUDA-resident solve backward, CUDA matrix_norm via resident composition, matrix_power via PyTorch-style identity/solve/matmul composition, tensorsolve via reshape+solve, tensorinv via reshape+solve(A,I), CPU svdvals via SVD's S backward, cond p=+/-2 via svdvals. Remaining unsupported tracked linalg paths now explicitly refuse to return detached tensors.","created_at":"2026-06-16T19:47:19.177380437Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAWibIzzZG5C6kuN+XXhhFeXMdpggRWYwMcr0PXyt25XhAEyl1pSe430ggRPTwsD2gmArnOHAW+tdgNzBv7R8aDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOqIR9c/yELMfj7HCDHtAea7VLwFDpYF2N2DqtF29CpOPNPpXq2eJzRQrdvlgdxHq5dFaIg1hP69LDDnWNpFuAA="}
