{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":338,"timestamp":"2026-06-16T22:04:35.498150487Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b81385cc-241c-4969-9059-920d291c1326","title":"CORE linalg norm/rank CUDA and dtype contract still trails PyTorch","description":"Follow-up found during the CORE-146 linalg sweep after fixing torch.linalg.cross. Current ferrotorch-core/src/linalg.rs still has vector_norm, cond, and matrix_rank behind require_cpu gates. PyTorch 2.11 supports torch.linalg.vector_norm and torch.linalg.matrix_rank on CUDA; matrix_rank also returns an int64 tensor on the input device, while ferrotorch matrix_rank currently returns a scalar encoded as Tensor<T>. This needs a resident CUDA implementation and an API/dtype contract review instead of CPU fallback or detached passthrough.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"b1cbe2a0-f4c4-4b35-b30b-2fbe693901bf","created_by":"y4rr"},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCluoXv+LoM+97c4F+FVxPjkL2PCtuUZNiFC9Yg6Kqklf1jvR+eEhs0V8A5NLbCcUHpxwfflFs6Y1pwveQ1HJAI="}
