{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":451,"timestamp":"2026-06-17T13:48:32.281557175Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9d7c925b-e8b6-4206-b2a3-257f19f43781","comment_uuid":"6a5ce598-923e-4c80-bd62-8186c84b2847","author":"y4rr","content":"Plan: inspect ferrotorch-core special.rs lgamma implementation and local PyTorch lgamma/native unary behavior for non-positive integer poles; verify whether f32/f64 both return +inf at exact negative integers while non-integer negatives keep reflection results; then patch the scalar path used by CPU/GPU fallbacks without broadening to unrelated beta/log_beta behavior. Add audit tests for negative-integer poles, nearby non-poles, dtype coverage, and downstream multigammaln/beta expectations if affected. Run fmt, focused tests, core lib tests, GPU-feature lib tests where relevant, strict clippy, then close and commit.","created_at":"2026-06-17T13:48:32.278195994Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAHkwbgbJd+uCVYzD3bpESWtXcyNT+0n/ZO2o7MSHD1lPpcOtvreWaCrar8q0MdD3wESZuwI6Qd6JTlKKAAV3qBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP4xJO3WAAFI/xdjUANSzJIGM+f2rJxJ+CRmXgXcMxdpbG9i+ZlNA0vNN3bYbC7d/nNqzaHWDXitK0nWH1jvuAI="}
{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":452,"timestamp":"2026-06-17T13:52:16.969093128Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9d7c925b-e8b6-4206-b2a3-257f19f43781","comment_uuid":"5f492df3-4723-4a8c-9cda-f3bf96cdbbab","author":"y4rr","content":"Observation: ferrotorch lgamma_scalar used Lanczos reflection for x < 0.5 and only checked sin(pi*x) == 0, so exact negative integers escaped as tiny rounded-pi sine residuals. Local PyTorch CPU source registers lgamma via IMPLEMENT_FLOAT_KERNEL_WITH_AVX512(lgamma) and special_gammaln is an alias to self.lgamma(); CUDA dispatches through lgamma_kernel_cuda. Live PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130 returns +inf for -0.0, +0.0, -1, -2, and -100 in f32/f64, while -0.5 and -1.5 remain finite.","created_at":"2026-06-17T13:52:16.966808313Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA81tWKjpBqLuuAs6QTSm3m6ZxSln1BPDLPVZLD01tJlQ8u/H66FmFFAAHXkmfeM5BDReUluZUE1ymx2k8qmM1AA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAF9+GXAtW6dnAJQ0ScvZvbmPuv6EECMMRK7dYPo6g54V15oZ9ctSgj41fts2sBkBPWnfwoXjcpC48obBtzeCwE="}
