{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":456,"timestamp":"2026-06-17T13:58:19.909010664Z","event":{"type":"IssueUpdated","uuid":"1affa82f-2d2c-4b13-86df-96c6b0b5a216","description":"Regression reopened from closed CORE-045/#1739 while verifying #1946.\n\nFailing command:\n`cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --features gpu --test conformance_activation -- --nocapture`\n\nCurrent failures:\n- `gpu_relu6`\n- `gpu_leaky_relu`\n- `gpu_hardtanh`\n- `gpu_hardsigmoid`\n- `gpu_hardswish`\n- `gpu_selu`\n- `gpu_softsign`\n- `gpu_softplus`\n- `gpu_hardtanh_with_custom_bounds`\n- `gpu_prelu`\n\nEach failure is a forward-path `NotImplementedOnCuda { op: \"unary_map\" }`.\n\nRoot cause from current source: `ops::elementwise::unary_map_named` is now intentionally CPU-only for CUDA tensors, but `grad_fns/activation.rs` still routes these activation forwards through `unary_map`; previous comments claiming a documented host round trip are stale. The grad-enabled half was covered by `audit_core045_activation_cuda_grad`, but no-grad CUDA forward coverage now exposes the resident-kernel gap.\n\nPyTorch parity requires real CUDA-resident forwards/backwards, not CPU passthroughs. Fix by adding named CUDA paths/kernels for the affected activations and updating comments/tests so the feature-gated conformance runner is green."},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEQcUzqnR0LR8t31MpGJZIQTZjIOAiJCX3s6Nd1dwbS1X7uhXwViWdysMLE4CS41kV1n4DEf3G5BXnLHdCncDQ0="}
{"agent_id":"y4rr","agent_seq":457,"timestamp":"2026-06-17T13:59:03.228051559Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9d7c925b-e8b6-4206-b2a3-257f19f43781","comment_uuid":"348df128-877b-48e3-8e31-422741c77cee","author":"y4rr","content":"Result: fixed lgamma negative-integer pole handling by guarding exact non-positive integers before the rounded-pi reflection branch, so -0.0, +0.0, -1, -2, and -100 return positive infinity like PyTorch/C99 instead of large finite values. Added the torch.special.gammaln-style alias as a direct wrapper over lgamma and re-exported it at crate root. Added audit_core194_lgamma_poles coverage for f64/f32 poles, nearby negative non-integers, root gammaln alias, and multigammaln pole propagation. Verification passed: cargo fmt --all; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --test audit_core194_lgamma_poles -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --test audit_core174_lgamma_inf -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --test audit_core173_digamma_poles -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --test conformance_activation -- --nocapture; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --lib; cargo test -p ferrotorch-core --features gpu --lib; cargo clippy -p ferrotorch-core --all-targets -- -D warnings; cargo clippy -p ferrotorch-core --all-targets --features gpu -- -D warnings. Additional optional GPU activation conformance run exposed unrelated regression #1995, filed separately for immediate follow-up.","created_at":"2026-06-17T13:59:03.225656220Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc85gQwD/Zjt8AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAJZ7zBenr4Q4M8OQoyXdiAFQU0IVML3XsnLLCbqELXkKcUeXbfZGf1jpntE28DSGZSYRdJDGTelza2cmkABKzBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:YWYNpJtV657L1tj0WNsAvmVQrz2HbQJv93mZZEx602c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/HKsBzj3mGAfTiSH5AbOUsF4b5ilHAPc8